{
  "version": 1,
  "notes": "Chern insulator (Haldane model)\nSpinless electrons on the honeycomb lattice with the Haldane coupling and a sublattice imbalance smaller than it: a Chern insulator. Bands (c1), the Chern number (c2) and the Berry curvature over the Brillouin zone, peaked at the K points (c3). Make the imbalance larger than about 5 times the Haldane coupling and the Chern number drops to zero. The phase diagram (c4) sweeps the Chern number (c2) over the imbalance and the Haldane coupling: the lobes of Chern number +1 and -1 are bounded by the lines where the gap closes, |mass| = 3 sqrt(3) |t|; it runs c2 at each of the 117 points (about ten seconds).",
